Long SECRET ident (same N on `println` / `eprintln`; refuse after parse — no full body emit):

| N | println emit sec / RSS | eprintln emit sec / RSS | println check sec / RSS | eprintln check sec / RSS |
|--:|-----------------------:|------------------------:|------------------------:|-------------------------:|
| 64 | 0.02 / 4920 | 0.02 / 4792 | 0.01 / 5692 | 0.01 / 5564 |
| 256 | 0.04 / 6200 | 0.04 / 6200 | 0.05 / 7012 | 0.04 / 6864 |
| 1024 | 0.38 / 11444 | 0.32 / 11312 | 0.36 / 11824 | 0.37 / 11712 |
| 2048 | 1.21 / 18104 | 1.27 / 18360 | 1.27 / 18168 | 1.32 / 18220 |

**Read:** println **tracks eprintln** (4.9 → 6.2 → 11.4 → 18.1 MB emit). Linear in ident/source, **not** a 2.9 concat bomb. Time 1024→2048 ≈ 3.2–4.0× for 2× N — `char_at` / lex (same as s61 H2 / s71 H2). emit-c **output size is ~constant** (8.2 → 10.2 KB) — refuse dies at preamble + `ERR secret`; the N-char ident is **not** copied into a growing C args buffer.

Many public idents (`let a0000 = 0; …; println|eprintln(a0000, …)`) — eprintln pays `c_emit_call_args` join + `c_guard_scan_idents`; println pays per-arg `oo_print_int` and **no** join:

| N | src B | println emit sec / RSS / C B | eprintln emit sec / RSS / C B | println check sec / RSS | eprintln check sec / RSS |
|--:|------:|-----------------------------:|------------------------------:|------------------------:|-------------------------:|
| 64 | ~1750 | 0.52 / 26296 / 12241 | 0.55 / 26552 / 11213 | 0.56 / 46536 | 0.54 / 46540 |
| 200 | ~5520 | 9.05 / 142648 / 19005 | 9.18 / 143800 / 15801 | 5.34 / 265008 | 5.19 / 264756 |
| 400 | ~11120 | 64.62 / 491956 / 29005 | *(killed mid-preamble; not re-run)* | 37.77 / 907100 | — |

**Read:** at N=64 and N=200, eprintln (full guard + join) is **+0.2–1.2 MB** vs println — noise vs the **token-list / let-env** driver (~63 KB·N class, same as s71 idents). eprintln C text is **smaller** (one `eprintln(a0, a1, …)` vs N `oo_print_int`). N=400 println check **907 MB** is the s71 `lets_N` emit thrash (env put / stmt list), **not** a walker concat. Do **not** attribute it to 2.9.

**H2 heap: PASS. H2 time: residual.** Unifying stmt println onto the eprintln rail would **not** change RSS class (join already cheaper than per-arg print). It would still be a **new join on that path** if DE copies `args = args + ", " + a` into `c_emit_println` — that copy is the H3 fail.

